  message: "id-format:F3 round-trip canary landed (PR #227, dev 05b8fd9cc9). The ADR-0036 Ruling-2 round-trip validator (_check_id_roundtrip in spec_validator.py, wired into validate_ir) now SURFACES and MEASURES the node.id kind-slot escapes at advisory (warning) severity: kind-slot not in the symbol-kind registry, and kind-slot != Symbol.kind. Behavioral evidence on merged dev: the tsconfig node (id kind-slot 'tsconfig', Symbol.kind 'file' — invisible to axis_conformance) and the external_symbol cohort (id 'go:fmt:0-0:Println:unresolved') both fire; the schema-coverage-corpus ratchet pins +11 such warnings. INV-dulah STAYS violated: the canary measures the cohort, but the producer folds that drain it to zero are id-changing (T1) and ride the v6 bump — WI-pubiv (external_symbol), WI-kugaj (route/event role), and the tsconfig fold (audit-findings 0005). Closes on the validated zero-violation cohort run after those folds, at which point the advisory checks promote to error (gating item WI-popak-gugoz-kibah-dugur-hopif-dutor-zopud-tamak). Deferred F3 sub-checks: Ruling-3 sentinel enumeration (WI-dipim..., T0) and Ruling-1 producer name sanitization (WI-sikar..., T1)."  # 30c5
