- op: discuss  # 6001
  at: '2026-06-22T04:47:28Z'  # 6001
  by: agent  # 6001
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 6001
  clock: 15  # 6001
  nonce: '6001'  # 6001
  message: "SCOPE ADDITION (human-directed, post-PR #4263): fold in the doc/markup/template-analyzer node-id DRY refactor here, because it changes node.id format (this invariant's axis). Context: WI-rijup canonicalized *stable_id* across 9 analyzers (rst/scss/vue/svelte/puppet/robot/astro/twig/pony) but deliberately left node.id and the 9 near-duplicate per-analyzer _make_symbol_id raw-id builders untouched (stable_id-scoped PR). The follow-up: (1) add a shared make_doc_symbol_ids(language, path, kind, name, start_line, end_line) -> (id, stable_id) helper in analyze/base.py that mints BOTH ids together so they can never drift again (the exact bug class WI-rijup fixed -- stable_id was set to the raw id); (2) dedup the 9 _make_symbol_id copies through it; (3) the 6 line-bearing analyzers (scss/vue/svelte/puppet/astro/twig) adopt it with ZERO node.id change (their id is already lang:path:kind:line:name, == helper output when line==span.start_line -- verify per site); (4) the 3 line-LESS analyzers (rst/robot/pony) currently emit lang:path:kind:name (no line) -- unifying them ADDS the line to node.id, which both conforms toward the documented id grammar (INV-dulah) AND fixes their latent same-name-sibling node.id collision. 'We'll get to it when we get to it.'"  # 6001
- op: discuss  # b7bd
  at: '2026-06-22T16:27:03Z'  # b7bd
  by: agent  # b7bd
  actor: jgstern_agent  # b7bd
  clock: 16  # b7bd
  nonce: b7bd  # b7bd
  message: "INV-dulah DRY refactor (the 2026-06-22 scope addition) DONE — merged to dev 469243b7b0. Added make_doc_symbol_ids(language, path, kind, name, start_line, end_line) -> (node_id, stable_id) in analyze/base.py: mints BOTH ids from one argument set so they can no longer drift (the WI-rijup bug class where 9 analyzers shipped stable_id == raw id), and dedups the 11 per-analyzer _make_symbol_id copies onto it (rst/robot/scss/vue/svelte/puppet/astro/pony/twig/sparql/kdl). node.id shape is {language}:{path}:{kind}:{start_line}:{name}. The 6 line-bearing analyzers + kdl: node.id byte-identical (verified per call site). The 4 line-less analyzers (rst/robot/pony/sparql): node.id GAINS the start_line segment, fixing their latent same-name-sibling node.id collision; stable_id unchanged. sparql uses_vocabulary edge dst now references the prefix node own id (prefix Symbols indexed by name in Pass 1). markdown/gitignore NOT folded — they already use a different, more grammar-conformant shape {lang}:{path}:{start-end}:{name}:{kind}. Adversarial all-kinds check (throwaway script + strengthened per-analyzer shape asserts): every non-file doc symbol node.id == {lang}:{path}:{kind}:{start_line}:{name}; 10343 passed, 100% coverage on changed sources.\n\nNEW PROPERTY of this invariant (pre-existing, NOT introduced by the refactor): the robot test_case node carries id/stable_id kind-slot 'test_case' while Symbol.kind == 'test' — a kind-slot vs Symbol.kind mismatch, same class as this invariant. The refactor faithfully preserved it (the helper kind arg mirrors the old make_doc_stable_id arg, so stable_id stayed byte-identical and node.id only gained the line).\n\nSTATUS stays VIOLATED: the DRY refactor prevents drift and fixes the collision but does NOT resolve the node.id-format invariant. The dominant cohorts persist — external_symbol nodes with 'unresolved' in the kind-slot, route IDs, and the doc-family slot ORDER is still kind:line:name rather than the documented span:name:kind grammar (full grammar conformance for the doc family is a separate, larger re-keying decision)."  # b7bd
