- op: discuss  # ef20
  at: '2026-07-29T11:13:19Z'  # ef20
  by: agent  # ef20
  actor: jgstern_agent  # ef20
  clock: 21  # ef20
  nonce: ef20  # ef20
  message: "ADVANCED, NOT CLOSED — the route-marker limb is fully drained; a DIFFERENT\nfamily remains live. Re-measured on self-analysis after the WI-zugob sweep\nrather than inferred from it, which is the point: route markers being clean says\nnothing about an umbrella whose scope is fleet-wide id-format conformance.\n\nFresh self-analysis validation_report (2026-07-29, dev at 539033b334):\n\n    total violations   18\n      cross_field  info      9\n      id_format    warning   8\n      id_format    error     1\n\nThe 9 id_format violations are ALL non-route, in two families:\n\nFAMILY 1 — the `script` kind-slot fossil (8 warnings, the bulk).\n    \"Symbol.id kind-slot 'script' does not match Symbol.kind 'file'\"\n    \"Symbol.id kind-slot 'script' is not a registered symbol-kind\"\n  Producer: json_config.py:253 —\n    _make_symbol_id(rel_path, start, end, script_name, \"script\")\n  while the record's kind is `file`. This is EXACTLY the shape WI-zugob just\n  drained for routes: a role written into the id kind-slot while Symbol.kind\n  carries the canonical value, and the role-word is not a registered kind. The\n  role already has a documented home — `meta[\"entry_role\"]=\"script\"` — which\n  noise_filter.py:15 and selection/filters.py:87 both read, so the fix is the\n  same shape as the route fold (keep the role in meta, put the symbol's own kind\n  in the slot) and needs no new vocabulary.\n\nFAMILY 2 — a malformed span segment (1 error, the only error-severity one).\n    \"Symbol.id does not match the canonical schema: malformed_span_segment\n     ('org.springframework.boot')\"\n  A package name is sitting where `{start}-{end}` belongs, so the id cannot be\n  parsed back into its slots — the same hard-grammar-break class as WI-javag's\n  6-segment Django id, not a slot-content mismatch. Candidate producers by grep:\n  java.py / linkers/jackson_dispatch.py / profile.py.\n\nBoth are the same generalisation the route sweep proved out: a producer\nhand-rolling an id writes a ROLE or an arbitrary string into a slot the grammar\nreserves for something else. The remedy shape is settled (a minting chokepoint\nthat derives the id from the record's own fields), so neither needs a new\ndesign decision — only the producer work and a gate that measures it first.\n\nNOT closing on \"routes are clean\". Per the closure-evidence discipline this\ninvariant's statement is about node.id fleet-wide, so its close condition is a\nfleet-wide measurement, and that measurement currently shows 9 violations."  # ef20
