  clock: 22  # 484a
  nonce: 484a  # 484a
  message: "MANIFEST-ANALYZER LIMB CLOSED; invariant stays violated on two other limbs (commit db6a80636a).\n\nFixed six sites across the three manifest analyzers, in two families. (a) Four kind-slot ROLE fossils: toml_config (pyproject [project.scripts]) and json_config (package.json scripts, package.json main, composer.json project) wrote the role/ecosystem -- script, main_entry, composer_package -- into the id kind-slot while Symbol.kind was file or package, so the id round-tripped to the wrong record and named an unregistered kind. Each role already had a consumer-read home (meta.entry_role, meta.package_ecosystem), so the fold is lossless. (b) Two Maven coordinate name-slots: xml_config's dependency and project symbols put groupId:artifactId into the name slot verbatim; because the parse is right-anchored (span,name,kind = parts[-3:]) that colon shifts every anchor and the id stops parsing. Both now use sanitize_id_name_segment, the scoped pattern the six synthetic-linker families already use.\n\nBEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE (re-ran the item's own repro): fresh self-analysis over 40841 symbols, id_format 9 -> 0 (8 warnings + the 1 error the ratchet baseline recorded as a known open Ruling-1 follow-up since 2026-07-02). Both baseline cells ratchet to 0. 11918 tests pass, 100% coverage on changed sources. Gated by a new 17-case property test over all three analyzers with a non-vacuity guard.\n\nWHY THIS IS NOT A CLOSE -- and specifically why the 0 must NOT be read as one. The statement enumerates four surviving limbs. Two are now done (route kind-slot WI-zugob; linker name-slot WI-vuzaf, both last session). The other two are NOT, and the 0 is silent on both:\n  - DOC-FAMILY SLOT ORDER (base.py make_doc_symbol_ids, 11 analyzers) still emits {lang}:{path}:{kind}:{start_line}:{name} -- span second-to-last, kind third -- deliberately not the ADR-0036 order. This limb is UNEXERCISED on the self-corpus: zero of the eleven file types (rst/scss/vue/svelte/pp/robot/pony/twig/rq/kdl) are tracked in this repo, so the measurement never reached it. Reading 'id_format 0' as evidence about this limb would be exactly the proxy-closure the closure-evidence discipline exists to prevent.\n  - WI-banod T1's 5 stable_ids remain, and are release-gated behind the WI-talos v9/v10 sequencing (register pt.33).\n\nScope note on the fix itself: only the toml site was firing on this corpus; main_entry and composer_package were found by auditing all three producers rather than by reading the violation list. Violation counts report what a corpus happens to exercise; a producer audit reports what exists."  # 484a
- op: discuss  # 2018
  at: '2026-07-30T07:13:12Z'  # 2018
  by: agent  # 2018
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2018
  clock: 23  # 2018
  nonce: '2018'  # 2018
  message: "DOC-FAMILY SLOT-ORDER LIMB CLOSED; CONFIG FAMILY FOLDED IN; TWO LIMBS REMAIN (PR #78, dev d0e45ce33b).\n\nThe doc-family limb named in this statement (\"the doc-family slot ORDER 'lang:path:kind:line:name' (base.py:983, deliberately not span-third/kind-last)\") is drained. make_doc_symbol_ids now DELEGATES to make_symbol_id instead of re-implementing the grammar in a local f-string, so all eleven adopters (rst/scss/vue/svelte/puppet/robot/pony/twig/sparql/kdl/astro) emit the canonical ADR-0036 shape at once -- a chokepoint, not a per-site sweep.\n\nMEASURED, not inferred. This limb was UNEXERCISED on the self-corpus for TWO compounding reasons, only one of which was recorded here, which is why the 2026-07-29 'id_format 0' said nothing about it: (a) zero of the eleven file types are tracked in this repo; (b) even with such files present the default pipeline FILTERS these node kinds, so include_docs=True is load-bearing (rst emits 2 sections through analyze_rst and 0 through a default run_behavior_map). On a generated 14-case corpus through the full pipeline: 34 non-canonical ids -> 0. Every one was malformed_span_segment -- the kind word sat where {start}-{end} belongs, so the ids did not parse into their slots at all.\n\nIDENTITY-SAFE: stable_id is computed from the same argument set either way, so it is byte-identical; no *_scheme bump (scheme-bump principle -- a bump follows an ALTERED existing computed value). No SCHEMA_VERSION change.\n\nFOUND BY GREP, NOT BY THE GATE: ini, requirements and properties each carried a PRIVATE COPY of the same broken shape (requirements/properties at only FOUR segments, no span at all), so they were invisible to any measurement scoped to the shared helper's callers. All three now mint through it; their three _make_symbol_id copies are deleted. Two requirements sites also dropped a kind-slot ROLE fossil (url_requirement / editable while Symbol.kind is requirement) -- the same lossless fold the manifest analyzers used, roles kept in meta.source_type / meta.editable.\n\nWHY THIS IS NOT A CLOSE. Two limbs remain, neither touched by the above:\n  - WI-banod T1's five sites (bitbake.py 192/302/342/382, bibtex.py 125 -- re-verified live, exactly the set WI-talos Ruling 3 enumerates) set stable_id = symbol_id. The composite id IS their stable identity, so correcting node.id CHANGES stable_id and falsifies v9's unqualified digest-compatibility claim. Blocked on a RELEASE, not on effort.\n  - Two kind-slot holes held as strict xfails in the new gate, both scheme-gated for the same reason (the kind arg feeds make_doc_stable_id): pony emits kind='actor' (unregistered) and robot passes kind='test_case' while building a kind='test' Symbol (a property recorded on this item since 2026-06-22).\n\nGate: packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_doc_family_id_parity.py -- 14 generated single-language cases, two properties each with measured strict-xfail hole sets. Corpus generated into tmp_path rather than committed: committing it added 1 axis_conformance error + 3 id_format warnings to the self-tree ratchet, because this gate deliberately preserves two producer defects. A gate that preserves a defect cannot host its corpus inside the tree the project ratchets against itself.\n\nNot closing on 'the doc family is clean' -- the statement is about node.id fleet-wide, so the close condition is a fleet-wide measurement."  # 2018
