    title: "node.id format escapes documented grammar — LIVE via 5 stable_ids (WI-banod T1, release-gated) + pony/robot kind-slot holes (scheme-gated); route ids, linker name-slots, doc-family slot-ORDER, manifest role fossils all DRAINED; external_symbol cohort FIXED, Rust '::' by-design"  # 9bd3
    fields:  # 9bd3
      statement: "node.id is documented as 'lang:path:span:name:kind'. SCOPE (2026-07-30 re-scope; supersedes the 2026-07-21 audit framing, which enumerated four surviving limbs of which THREE are now drained): the dominant historical breakage -- ~1663 external_symbol nodes carrying 'unresolved' in the kind-slot -- was FIXED by WI-pubiv (df8e1e60da, 2026-07-02; ir.py:1273 now emits the external_symbol kind-slot), and the Rust '::'->'.' name-slot case is by-design per ADR-0036 Ruling-1 (WI-nagub wont_do).\n\nDRAINED SINCE THE 2026-07-21 AUDIT: (a) route id kind-slot (WI-zugob); (b) linker name-slot constants (WI-vuzaf); (c) the doc-family slot ORDER (PR #78, dev d0e45ce33b, 2026-07-30 -- make_doc_symbol_ids now DELEGATES to make_symbol_id rather than re-implementing the grammar, so all eleven adopters conform at one chokepoint, and the ini/requirements/properties private copies fold in with it); (d) the manifest-analyzer role fossils + Maven coordinate name-slots found alongside them (db6a80636a; self-analysis id_format 9 -> 0).\n\nTWO LIMBS REMAIN, and a fleet-wide id_format of 0 is SILENT on both -- reading that 0 as a close would be exactly the proxy closure the closure-evidence discipline exists to prevent:\n  1. WI-banod T1's five stable_id = symbol_id sites (bitbake.py 192/302/342/382, bibtex.py 125 -- re-verified live 2026-07-30, exactly the set WI-talos Ruling 3 enumerates). The composite id IS their stable identity, so correcting node.id CHANGES stable_id and falsifies v9's unqualified digest-compatibility claim. Blocked on a RELEASE, not on effort (v9/v10 sequencing, register pt.33).\n  2. Two kind-slot holes held as strict xfails in packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_doc_family_id_parity.py, both scheme-gated for the same reason (the kind arg feeds make_doc_stable_id): pony emits kind='actor' (unregistered symbol-kind) and robot passes kind='test_case' while building a kind='test' Symbol (a property recorded on this item since 2026-06-22).\n\nCLOSE CONDITION: a fleet-wide measurement, not a per-family 0. The original 2026-06 framing (12 nodes: npm 3-colon, Rust '::', route colon-prefix, Solidity carry-over) and the 2026-07-21 four-limb framing are preserved in git history and in this discussion thread."  # 9bd3
- op: discuss  # e2e6
